{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris","id":378460,"title":"A Werewolf Chronicle In Paris","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-22T17:02:02-08:00","id":378460,"title":"A Werewolf Chronicle In Paris","content":"So my next Werewolf game (and my first with the post-playtest, proper Idigam Chronicle 2e ruleset) is going to be set in Paris.<br /> <br /> I have some ideas of where I'm going to go with things, but I'm interested in sounding out the forum's ideas and inspirations.<br /> <br /> What should feature in a Paris Werewolf chronicle? What are cool locations, interesting bits of culture and really cool elements of folklore and urban myth that should definitely be included? What are the obvious spiritual hotspots and centres of occult weirdness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:34:45-08:00","id":378536,"title":"","content":"The Catacombs.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I couldn't imagine a WoD game without those catacombs. There HAS to be something important to Death Wolf down there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T18:43:18-08:00","id":378573,"title":"","content":"absolutely the catacombs, but also the french country side since the loup-garou as an ever popular ame comes from there. Emphasize the human fear of the night and the furred beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T19:09:31-08:00","id":378600,"title":"","content":"I haven't been there in decades, but all I really recall was people were pretty nice.<br /> <br /> I know there's a lot of rats there, now. Like, several times the population of people. And obviously there's the political climate. From a World of Darkness standpoint it would be a hot spot for Fire-Touched and beshilu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:13:57-08:00","id":378623,"title":"","content":"Is it gonna be played online? I'd love to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:16:41-08:00","id":378628,"title":"","content":"France has Gauls/Normans background, and there is large portion of pagan believes, even if they are mostly now Catholic or Agnostic. But for millennium Church was very big part of French identity. Nice touch would be local alternative Pangea myth, maybe more based on Garden of Eden and First Sin? You could based it on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298515#post298515\">mine for Old Testament sketch</a>. With Death Wolf involvement with Catacombs, maybe Firstborns could make larger presence in those local tales? Waiting to read from you on this topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's more? Oh, yes. Gargoyles - always loved them! &lt;3 In <b>Changeling</b> there is Banished Fae that talks with Gargoyles, in <b>Autumn Nightmares</b> if I remember good. In <b>Werewolf</b>, I would make them spirits of specific Choir that are mythical beings, but also object spirits. And they are <b>not</b> Magath. And they are watching <i>everything</i>, for <i>centuries</i>. And they are weird and powerful in local Shadow.<br /> <br /> Old Town with truly Gothic buildings. Huge social disproportions of previous centuries, that picked in times of French Revolution ( i.e. <i>Assasin's Creed Unity</i> ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Garou ( Big Bad Wolf ) as major legend of <b>\u00cele-de-France region</b> ( that Paris is center of ). There is even a story of local werewolf trials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/op4inSVZugU?t=8m47s\" data-code=\"op4inSVZugU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/op4inSVZugU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Some culture works I would look on your place... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/VtdbyugYO7A\" data-code=\"VtdbyugYO7A\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VtdbyugYO7A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/PCfVR1R9L6E\" data-code=\"PCfVR1R9L6E\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PCfVR1R9L6E/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/UB-87ySgVY0\" data-code=\"UB-87ySgVY0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UB-87ySgVY0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Hopes it all helps you and wait to see more interesting stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-22-2015, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:16:55-08:00","id":378629,"title":"","content":"Anyhow, Underworld-touched Beshilu nesting on the catacombs erupting and making zombies with their bites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:49:02-08:00","id":378641,"title":"","content":"Take &quot;As above so below&quot; as an example (fun movie too!). The Beshilu can be gnawing holes in the gauntlet in the catacombs. Explorers take a wrong turn and find themselves in the hisil... hallucinations? Maybe...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T21:22:33-08:00","id":378713,"title":"","content":"Leftover violence spirits from the French Revolution, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T04:45:51-08:00","id":378891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378713#post378713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leftover violence spirits from the French Revolution, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... those would have evolved in 200 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T04:57:05-08:00","id":378896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378536#post378536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Catacombs.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I couldn't imagine a WoD game without those catacombs. There HAS to be something important to Death Wolf down there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no doubt the catacombs will feature. Sadly it doesn't look like the pack will include any Bone Shadows <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378573#post378573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">absolutely the catacombs, but also the french country side since the loup-garou as an ever popular ame comes from there. Emphasize the human fear of the night and the furred beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question is, how likely is it that the Uratha in Paris will have territories that spread out far into the countryside out of the capital?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378600#post378600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't been there in decades, but all I really recall was people were pretty nice.<br /> <br /> I know there's a lot of rats there, now. Like, several times the population of people. And obviously there's the political climate. From a World of Darkness standpoint it would be a hot spot for Fire-Touched and beshilu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, planning to make heavy use of both of those. I have a soft spot for beshilu in general, but I'd also like to bring azlu to bear as I've generally underused them in previous games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378623#post378623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it gonna be played online? I'd love to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a face-to-face game with my regular group. We'll probably podcast it once the 2e corebook is released though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378628#post378628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nice touch would be local alternative Pangea myth, maybe more based on Garden of Eden and First Sin?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm probably not going to run with an alternative Pangaea myth, I do plan on mucking about with some of the folklore by threading it into the Uratha. Probably go with the idea of the link between witches and werewolves being played up heavily, among other things, and use King Philip the Fair vs the Templars as the spark of something interesting that one of the Tribes draws on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378629#post378629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow, Underworld-touched Beshilu nesting on the catacombs erupting and making zombies with their bites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, zombie-making Beshilu is an amusing idea. There's certainly scope to pull in Underworld-related stuff, so I'll probably make use of my 2e-ified version of the Lodge of Death, maybe even use Geists at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378641#post378641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take &quot;As above so below&quot; as an example (fun movie too!). The Beshilu can be gnawing holes in the gauntlet in the catacombs. Explorers take a wrong turn and find themselves in the hisil... hallucinations? Maybe...</div> </div> </div> </div>The alchemical elements of that movie do offer an interesting thread to draw in as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=378713#post378713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leftover violence spirits from the French Revolution, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. Any violence spirit tough enough to have survived since the French Revolution is probably quite the heavyweight these days too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T10:00:47-08:00","id":381087,"title":"","content":"Right then, so having had some time to make notes and think, the very rough draft of where I think I'll go with the campaign. My players, obviously, keep out, you nosy sods <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My last big Werewolf campaign didn't feature any idigam, and now I have these shiny rules I've written for 2e I kinda want to put some idigam in. Thing is, my last big campaign *did* feature a rather idigam-<i>like </i>ancient spirit that had become Wounded by Baalphegor and had ended up wedged between the Spirit and the Underworld for various reasons. I don't want to do basically just a repeat of that.<br /> <br /> So I figure this time I'll use <i>two</i> idigam; two opposite sides of the coin, possibly in actual opposition. One at the centre of Cromlech lines that meet under Paris, an ancient Earth-Bound Coalesced from death and rot that has long since slumbered with its servants forming their own society and cult around it; now it slowly threatens to wake, bringing a swell in spiritual power that the werewolves are unable to explain but know they must contain. The other is high rather than deep, a Moon-Banished crafting itself a throne of data and technology amidst the tower-heights of La Defence, operating subtly for now as it gathers Essence and power. Where the High Cromlech is a behemoth of dark symbolism, the Data Angel is careful, measured, taking time to achieve its goals.<br /> <br /> Neither idigam will be a heavy player at the very beginning - the High Cromlech is asleep but stirring, while the Data Angel is taking every precaution it can, operating to be as deniable as possible. Things will slowly ramp up as the game progresses, but I'm looking at a mid-game state where one or both idigam becomes revealed even if not fully active yet. Their presence will be felt from early on, though, as their spawn begin to spread and the Hunting Ground begins to metamorphose from their influence.<br /> <br /> I'm looking at there being broadly four themes for the game - Fire, Death, Division and Transition.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire:</b> Anger, passion, emoiton, madness, revolution. A spark can lead to riots and literal flames, or unleash unfettered creativity. Fire changes and consumes; it unleashes energy. Paris is a place of fire, whether a night sky awash with illumination from the glowing city below or the ruddy embers of burning cars in the streets. Werewolves are creatures of fire; their rage and passions burn close to the surface. The Fire-Touched are strong here.<br /> <br /> <b>Death:</b> The heavy weight of history, pressing down on the landscape through layers of bones. Paris is saturated with death; cemetary upon cemetary, plague-graves, catacombs that worm beneath the city. The streets echo with the ghosts and whispers of past ages and lost souls. Memento Mori are everywhere. The werewolves are a part of that lineage, bearing relics and reminders of death from the past. Ancient parts of the city hold many mysteries; the dead often have the answers. The Bone Shadows are strong here.<br /> <br /> <b>Division:</b> Lines are drawn. Everyone is divided. The Forsaken are not unified. Two Protectorates lay claim to portions of Paris, each driven by different ideologies and crises. The Pure are not unified. A great fault line hangs between the Ivory Claws and the Fire-Touched. Yet other werewolves pay allegiance to the Lyceum, Apollo-worshipping heretics. Whispers speak of other, stranger wolf-cults. Paris is a place where innumerable times, places and peoples mix, but the lines between them are pronounced, and tensions are strong.<br /> <br /> <b>Transition:</b> Even where there are deep lines, it can be hard to know exactly where the boundaries lie. Territories are a patchwork of rival factions, and alleigance to one faction doesn't necessarily prevent alliance with another. Paris is a place of transition and change, spiritually and symbolically; Claimed stalk amongst the population, and Hosts leave the two worlds bleeding into each other. Time brings change to the city-scape, ancient buildings rubbing shoulders with the new. Bale Hounds foster covens of witches and cultists, teaching them rite-magic that should not be theirs.<br /> <br /> We've got three Uratha in the pack; a Storm Lord Irraka, Blood Talon Rahu and Iron Master (either an Ithaeur or an Elodoth), then one Wolf-Blooded player character as well (quite significantly souped-up to give him a better chance of keeping pace with the other pack members). Will be interesting to see how this turns out!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:14:59-08:00","id":381300,"title":"","content":"I'd love to play a Bone Shadow Cahalith there. Damn you for not having migrated to an online platform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:17:25-08:00","id":381303,"title":"","content":"I have to admit to being incredibly jealous of people playing 2e games already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:29:03-08:00","id":381308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381087#post381087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I figure this time I'll use <i>two</i> idigam; two opposite sides of the coin, possibly in actual opposition. One at the centre of Cromlech lines that meet under Paris, an ancient Earth-Bound Coalesced from death and rot that has long since slumbered with its servants forming their own society and cult around it; now it slowly threatens to wake, bringing a swell in spiritual power that the werewolves are unable to explain but know they must contain. The other is high rather than deep, a Moon-Banished crafting itself a throne of data and technology amidst the tower-heights of La Defence, operating subtly for now as it gathers Essence and power. Where the High Cromlech is a behemoth of dark symbolism, the Data Angel is careful, measured, taking time to achieve its goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for some reason, I can picture this easily fitting into a Demon game.<br /> <br /> The Idigam settling in deactivated infrastructure. Demon PCs go in expect Angels and normal G-M bits, only to encounter Moon-Banished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:46:56-08:00","id":381315,"title":"","content":"Or said Idigam could easily be (Arch?)Angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T14:26:56-08:00","id":381356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381300#post381300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to play a Bone Shadow Cahalith there. Damn you for not having migrated to an online platform.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still do pretty much all my gaming face-to-face. We did briefly use webcams and an online platform to play some Wolsung with a friend who was over in Portugal for a few years but I don't really enjoy the medium that much. That said, if we permanently move to Poland at some point I'll probably have to go to online methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381303#post381303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit to being incredibly jealous of people playing 2e games already.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, it's nice to play Werewolf again in a game where we aren't constantly having to check everything we do, running into errors and broken bits of the system, and can just <i>play</i> again. Playtesting really is work; now I get to actually have fun with all the stuff I helped write.<br /> <br /> There will be various bits of stuff that I'll have to wait til the corebook release before I can go into them here; once Werewolf 2e's out, for example, I'll likely do write-ups for the High Cromlech and the Data Angel.<br /> <br /> Currently, my next challenge is adding detail to the two Protectorates. One is based around the Zero Point at the city's heart, a coalition of packs trying to address the problem of the massive spiritual surge they can feel building up in Paris and seething across the Gauntlet. The Zero Point itself is the focus of this, and through extensive rituals, experiments and desperate methods the Zero Point Protectorate is bleeding off power and stopping what they expect will be the equivalent of a Shadow eruption. This Protectorate has strong links to lots of other Forsaken across France, through Tribal and Lodge networks, because the symbolism of Paris as the capital of France has an impact across the country; no French pack wants Paris to go horribly, spiritually wrong or even just physically explode. The second Protectorate, I think, will be the personal grudge match of two Forsaken elders who hate each other but are working together against the Pure, gathering the non-Zero Point packs (both Forsaken and Ghost Wolf) under their control through force of personality and strength of arms; while Zero Point hurl vast resources into stopping the eruption of whatever it is (it ultimately being, of course, the waking murmurs of the High Cromlech), the second Protectorate does a kinda taking-in-the-huddled-masses thing, gathering power and influence with the disaffected in order to war with the Pure and to erode the Zero Point Protectorate's power and influence.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Lyceum, actual worshippers of the Greek god Apollo in his aspect as a wolf. They see themselves as philosopher-kings, aesthetes, gourmets, enlightened types. Everyone else thinks they're pagan nutjobs. The Lyceum are a sorta hedonistic, Epicurean cult of pleasure and the hunt, believing themselves chosen to guard the treasures of a holy place of Apollo. They're Ghost Wolves technically, with the Lyceum being the Lodge that ties them together, but they are probably originally some sort of weird blend of a Hunter in Darkness sect with the influence of something else, possibly a Pure sect of some kind. They're no-where near as big as either Protectorate, but they have some serious and weird rite-magic at their fingertips and the aid of some very weird entities.<br /> <br /> I'll probably run with some other werewolf heretics as well, in the form of a ghoulish underground cult haunting the catacombs and sewers under Paris. They're basically just going to be one big pack of Ghost Wolves, all tied together into one weird Lodge that may well originally have been Bone Shadow. I'm tempted to have them as worshippers or attendants to some sort of shoggothian Lou Carcolh; I could just make them troglodytes, the equivalent of werewolf morlocks, but I want them to be less primitive and crude, more <i>weird</i> and devoted.<br /> <br /> Most of the other, 'regular' Ghost Wolves are getting hoovered up by the second Protectorate, but there's a good few small packs of them out in the banlieus still. These kinds of packs can literally have their own cult-like ideologies and believes that vary from one pack to the next, but the most common lore centres around Ys, the sunken city off France that was damned by Dahud and given to the Devil as a prize; the people of the city were cursed to become werewolves, so the Ghost Wolf cults claim. The Forsaken believe differently; they think Ys probably <i>was</i> real but may have been an actual community ruled by werewolves, attacked and destroyed by a powerful spirit that feared their power. I'll need to figure out the story of the place as, at some point, I think I might have Princess Dahud actually turn up.<br /> <br /> Finally on the 'non-Pure' roster, we have the Bale Hounds. The line between the Ghost Wolves and Bale Hounds is blurred; there are lots of Ghost Wolves that think they are damned by God and that the Devil is their master, and some of them have cults that grow up around them. The Bale Hounds are far more purposeful in how they foster cults and covens, though, actively gathering groups of humans and Wolf-Blooded to whom they can teach rites and occult secrets to further their plans. I used Pseulak and Baalphegor worshippers extensively before, so I'll probably go with Lamashtu this time, although I'm not yet sure how much importance the Bale Hounds will play in this game or whether anyone else will really make any differentiation between any of the 'mad werewolves gathering witch-cults' anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T14:54:00-08:00","id":381373,"title":"","content":"Concerning your murlock ghost wolves, it rang a few bells with the Lodge of the Grotto, from Faithful. Maybe you could adapt them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T15:51:23-08:00","id":381406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381356#post381356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it's nice to play Werewolf again in a game where we aren't constantly having to check everything we do, running into errors and broken bits of the system, and can just <i>play</i> again. Playtesting really is work; now I get to actually have fun with all the stuff I helped write.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking forward to it too, but I hope you keep us informed about your game, it sounds like the makings of a fun one. I like the Lyceum, and the other Protectorate and how its rivalry sort of detracts from Zero Point. And apparently Ys is more than a video game, who knew.<br /> <br /> Any idea if the wolf-blooded is going to turn later or do they, so far, intend to stay wolf-blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T02:12:55-08:00","id":381707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381356#post381356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do pretty much all my gaming face-to-face. We did briefly use webcams and an online platform to play some Wolsung with a friend who was over in Portugal for a few years but I don't really enjoy the medium that much. That said, if we permanently move to Poland at some point I'll probably have to go to online methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or I could have got you some local names for Polish players. Not to be too proud but I'm quasi recognizable in our local fandom. Just ask for &quot;Litwin from Lublin&quot; in Eastern Poland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Wolsung is evil - I wanted to play it 10 year ago, when it was in production. But when it finally came out it shown it was just historical rip-off just trying to be steampunk fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:55:29-08:00","id":381976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381373#post381373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning your murlock ghost wolves, it rang a few bells with the Lodge of the Grotto, from Faithful. Maybe you could adapt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a look at the Grotto but there's not really much to work from there, and what there is, is too 'primitive troglodyte' style for my tastes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381406#post381406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking forward to it too, but I hope you keep us informed about your game, it sounds like the makings of a fun one. I like the Lyceum, and the other Protectorate and how its rivalry sort of detracts from Zero Point. And apparently Ys is more than a video game, who knew.<br /> <br /> Any idea if the wolf-blooded is going to turn later or do they, so far, intend to stay wolf-blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Wolf-Blooded has every intention of remaining Wolf-Blooded for the duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381707#post381707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or I could have got you some local names for Polish players. Not to be too proud but I'm quasi recognizable in our local fandom. Just ask for &quot;Litwin from Lublin&quot; in Eastern Poland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Wolsung is evil - I wanted to play it 10 year ago, when it was in production. But when it finally came out it shown it was just historical rip-off just trying to be steampunk fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be in eastern Poland, I'm afraid :P There are local gamers around where we have a house, but my actual Polish remains not so great so I'd need a group of fluent English-speakers.<br /> <br /> Wolsung was ok, it just didn't really float my boat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:59:39-08:00","id":382050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=381976#post381976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be in eastern Poland, I'm afraid :P There are local gamers around where we have a house, but my actual Polish remains not so great so I'd need a group of fluent English-speakers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And were you are going to in Poland? I think me and my <b>Mage</b> group - that read sourcebooks for free time - I think we could make it work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:53:34-08:00","id":382339,"title":"","content":"If we move to Poland permanently at some point, it'll be to Wroclaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:25:30-08:00","id":382556,"title":"","content":"Don't do it man. From what I've read*, Wroclaw is all kinds of messed up!<br /> <br /> * My reading has been *extremely* limited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:33:28-08:00","id":382926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=382556#post382556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't do it man. From what I've read*, Wroclaw is all kinds of messed up!<br /> <br /> * My reading has been *extremely* limited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this qualifies you as a Bad Man or a Cryptic Hinter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, man, stay away from Wroclaw. Especially Psie Pole, that place sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T04:43:22-08:00","id":386145,"title":"","content":"Well, we've now had the proper character and pack creation session; the characters are all ready to go, we have an interesting totem, some fleshed-out links to the setting, and an interesting pack origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T04:48:36-08:00","id":386146,"title":"","content":"What's the totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:23:24-08:00","id":386184,"title":"","content":"It's the spirit of an old bronze foundry that once stood in the banlieu. The foundry has long since collapsed into ruin and decay, and the spirit only survived due to a locus of Metal on the site. Once a glorious monstrosity of white-hot liquid metal, fire and ash, it is now a lurching horror of smouldering embers and rust.<br /> <br /> The pack have taken it on as their totem because they want to see themselves as a renewing force in the banlieu that will help bring it back some of its former glory. I haven't yet settled on its personality etc or name, but I'm working on that.<br /> <br /> It also comes with a really quite harsh ban - they can't destroy objects of crafted metal. This will definitely cause them some issues... but if they're successful at sticking to it, that might help rekindle the totem's old flame more swiftly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:01:32-08:00","id":386259,"title":"","content":"Cool. Time to throw in an Unfleshed promethean. I really like the ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:25:08-08:00","id":386279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=386184#post386184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the spirit of an old bronze foundry that once stood in the banlieu. The foundry has long since collapsed into ruin and decay, and the spirit only survived due to a locus of Metal on the site. Once a glorious monstrosity of white-hot liquid metal, fire and ash, it is now a lurching horror of smouldering embers and rust.<br /> <br /> The pack have taken it on as their totem because they want to see themselves as a renewing force in the banlieu that will help bring it back some of its former glory. I haven't yet settled on its personality etc or name, but I'm working on that.<br /> <br /> It also comes with a really quite harsh ban - they can't destroy objects of crafted metal. This will definitely cause them some issues... but if they're successful at sticking to it, that might help rekindle the totem's old flame more swiftly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool ban. Reminds me that I'll need to figure out a ban for my Hope Totem. Did the players come up with the totem all their own or did you seed their fertile minds with some ideas beforehand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:45:22-08:00","id":386295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=386279#post386279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a really cool ban. Reminds me that I'll need to figure out a ban for my Hope Totem. Did the players come up with the totem all their own or did you seed their fertile minds with some ideas beforehand?</div> </div> </div> </div>The players did the vast bulk of it. I asked them whereabouts they wanted their territory, and they decided not to go in the Arrondisements of the central city but in the banlieus instead, one of the less wealthy places that would let us get at the themes of poverty, urban decay and ethnic tensions that plague some regions of Paris today. The ithaeur's player suggested their Safe Place merit and their locus be an old closed-down junkyard that his character (an artist) used as a source of metal for his sculptures, with the locus being a mass of twisted, amalgamated old metal that is of Metal resonance. From there, they decided they wanted their totem to be linked, somehow, to the post-industrial state of the area; I mentioned a factory or other industrial location, we talked about metal, then someone suggested a foundry. First suggestions were a steel foundry but I did a little research and found references to bronze foundries in the area, which they really liked.<br /> <br /> So they settled on the spirit being that of the old, collapsed bronze foundry, spent some time wondering about bans, and then I suggested the ban above that we all agreed on as an interesting and impactful one.<br /> <br /> Anyways, next up is weaving in the various NPCs suggested by the backstory and the Merit dots that the characters possess. I'll probably spread their links between the Point Zero protectorate and the Lamplighters protectorate to maximise the tensions and conflicting pulls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T10:50:22-08:00","id":386477,"title":"","content":"Given such a restrictive ban, how powerful is their totem? I really dig the fact that the their territory's in a banlieues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T12:18:37-08:00","id":386569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Crimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=386477#post386477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given such a restrictive ban, how powerful is their totem? I really dig the fact that the their territory's in a banlieues.</div> </div> </div> </div>The totem is, as yet, quite weak even despite the powerful ban. Still, it brings useful capabilities to the group.<br /> <br /> I think the banlieues provide an excellent setting for the pack's territory, and the broad distinction between the Point Zero protectorate (mostly in the arrondisements) and the Lamplighters protectorate (mostly in the banlieues) will provide a nice contrast. Still, the pack are close enough to the edge of the arrondisements that they could lean towards either protectorate politically. We'll see how it plays out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:45:59-08:00","id":386754,"title":"","content":"What counts as 'crafted' for that ban? Are they banned from using firearms because they're destroying crafted metal bullets into deformed slugs and casings? Or does it refer to hand crafted, rather than forged?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T16:19:19-08:00","id":386800,"title":"","content":"Hmm, yes, I might need to tighten up the definitions a bit. Perhaps instead, they can't destroy objects of crafted metal except for by the objects' design - so they can fire a bullet or crack open a can of whatever.<br /> <br /> It refers to any intentionally crafted metal object, whether manufactured or hand-crafted. Admittedly the firearms issue isn't really an issue for them since none of the pack use firearms and the ex-hunter Wolf-Blooded is using a bow (easier to deliver Bane payloads via arrow); besides, France gun control, while not as strict as for ex. the UK means that packing firearms is pretty tricky to get away with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T17:09:55-08:00","id":386853,"title":"","content":"If I could put in a small suggestion based upon my experience in Paris, your players could have a fantastic encounter at the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_Georges_Pompidou\" target=\"_blank\">Centre Pompidou</a>. I even recall you creating a really fun sounding library spirit in another thread on these forums that could fit in perfectly at that location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:36:10-08:00","id":387525,"title":"","content":"That might turn up at some stage if/when their ventures take them into the arrondisements. Currently, their territory is going to be in one of the banlieues of Bagnolet, Romainville or Montreuil, though I haven't decided which as yet, which puts them in the near east of the city.<br /> <br /> I've found the following map of the banlieues and arrondisements particularly useful, because it very nicely indicates the rich and poor areas of the city:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banlieue#mediaviewer/File:Revenus_%C3%A0_Paris_et_Petite_Couronne.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2018-0525-sous_l_eau-001.jpg/1280px-2018-0525-sous_l_eau-001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banlieue#mediaviewer/File:Revenus_%C3%A0_Paris_et_Petite_Couronne.JPG\" target=\"_blank\"> Banlieue - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banlieue#mediaviewer/File:Revenus_%C3%A0_Paris_et_Petite_Couronne.JPG\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banlieue#mediaviewer/File:Revenus_%C3%A0_Paris_et_Petite_Couronne.JPG </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T05:07:27-08:00","id":392511,"title":"","content":"So, the totem has ended up being called <i>Zabasimuthari </i>the Enduring Smith of Bronze. Once the 2e corebook is out, I'll post its stats up in the thread. Its Bane is currently copper chloride (causes 'bronze disease' and relatively easily accessible) because I couldn't think of a better one as yet :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T14:18:52-08:00","id":393030,"title":"","content":"The b<span style=\"font-size:12px\">elow is the intro document I've sent over to my players</span><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> for the Paris game. Nothing NDA-breaking in here.</span></span><b><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><br /> <br /> Werewolf: City of Light</span></b> <br /> This here's a rough intro/briefing document putting together what we've discussed so far, along with new details about the Uratha of Paris and the pack's territory. Any questions, queries or clarifications, don't hesitate to ask. Also, this stuff is obviously not set in stone; we can make changes and adjustments as desired.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Pack</span></b><br /> Written-in-Blood, Blood Talon Rahu, a wasted life remade in a moment of carnage.<br /> Bianca Louvier, Storm Lord Irraka, scion of a noted lineage who stalked the stalker 'neath the new moon.<br /> Howling Phantom, Bone Shadow Ithaeur, woken to deeper truths beneath the skin of Paris.<br /> Henri, Wolf-Blooded, a conspiracy's favoured weapon fled from its sheathe.<br /> <br /> 1 Wolf-Blooded pack member who is involved with Written-in-Blood, expert on cults who fell into the Changeling's web.<br /> 6 human pack members, lost sheep formerly of the Changeling's flock who are now all too aware of the darkness in the world.<br /> <br /> <i>Zabarsimuhthari </i>the Enduring Smith of Bronze, spirit of a crumbling foundry whose doors have long since shut.<br /> <br /> This is the pack as it stands at the beginning of the game.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Paris, City of Light</b></span><br /> Three Uratha, three Tribes, three different initiations that have revealed the world's true nature - the spirit world that lies alongside the flesh, the horrors that menace the Gauntlet and stalk the herd, and the ancient enmities that the Forsaken are caught up in.<br /> <br /> <b>Mentors &amp; Tutors</b><br /> Written-in-Blood has been mentored by a rahu called Noah Vengeance-in-Silver, so named for having killed an Ivory Claw in horrific fashion by pouring molten silver over the Anshega. Noah is a member of the Matagot lodge and, despite his Oath-breaking acts of terror, takes a very grim, even sin-eating approach to the task - his serious demeanour and relentless lessons about why <i>he</i> is damning himself so that other Forsaken need not be is considered by the Tribe to be a good crucible for new <i>Suthar Anzuth</i> to go through. Noah is a member of the Burning Ground, a pack with lineage back to WW2, they are part of the Lamplighter Protectorate and hold territory in the commune of Pantin.<br /> <br /> Howling Phantom has been mentored by an ithaeur called the Eaten Wolf, a blind shaman who has sold many parts of herself - both flesh and symbolic - in pacts with the spirits of Paris. One of these pacts sold her former names, and now no-one can even remember what her deed name used to be. She is extremely wise but the Tribe also consider her a good warning to new Bone Shadows of where to draw the line in dealings; her mutilated and scarified flesh, empty eye sockets and the befuddling amnesia that can cloud out parts of memories of her usually do that job well enough. The Eaten Wolf is part of the Tithed Scribes, a pack that holds the Memorial of Fighting France in the west suburbs and that includes several members of the Lodge of Death; the Scribes remain apart from allegiance to either Protectorate.<br /> <br /> Bianca has been mentored by the Storm Lord Cahalith called the Fishing Cat, known to Bianca more commonly as 'great-aunt Lucile'. Lucile is matriarch of the Louvier clan, a major bloodline of <i>Iminir</i> in Paris that is bound to always provide one of its number to a special bond with an eerie old spirit in the Street of the Fishing Cat in the 5th Arrondisement. This arrangement is a strange and symbiotic one, and Lucile has a particularly good sense of the spiritual currents of the city and urban courts in Paris; she is essentially in her own, personal Lodge. Lucile is one of the elders of the Zero Point Protectorate, and the Louvier pack hold portions of the 5th Arrondisement as their territory.<br /> <br /> Then there is Henri, part-wolf, no Tribe, sought by his former compatriots of the Office of Specific and Non-Specific Oversight, the off-the-books government hunter agency with a dark past and sinister practices, in deep with some sort of occult corporation called Cheiron. Still, he has one advantage - the ancestrally-bound spirit of dust, straw and guardianship that is always there for him. Henri still has problems wrapping his tongue round the spirit's 'real' name but it translates to Empty Dust.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore of Light</b><br /> As well as the knowledge that their tutors have imparted to them, there are other pieces of knowledge, rumours, advice and the like that have been passed on.<br /> <br /> France and Paris are both unusual in their own ways. France has far higher number of Uratha in its population that you'd expect, and this doesn't appear to be down to bloodlines or inheritance. It's <i>geographical</i>, with immigrant groups suffering the same increase in Uratha when they come to France, and emmigrants losing it in other lands. Paris itself has a very thin Gauntlet - in part due to centuries of Beshilu gnawing at it, the tumult of revolutions, the spiritual impressions of vast mass graves and the like. The Eaten Wolf implies that there is more to the Gauntlet's frailty, and that she knows why, but as yet does not reveal such secrets to Howling Phantom.<br /> <br /> Darkness and light play a key role in the spiritual ecology of the city. Not only are the broods of light and dark very powerful, but these symbols run through the agreements, pacts and rites of the Parisian <i>hisil</i>. Many packs have places in their territories that they must always keep lit or in darkness in order to adhere to strange Bans and laws of the Shadow. All of the mentors have made it clear that identifying the particular requirements of the local spirit ecology in terms of light and dark will be important to managing it and wielding power over it. The Lamplighters have taken their name from the belief that, unlike Zero Point, they hold up the wellbeing of the city and its Uratha.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, in the Shadow, areas of night-time Paris have their skies ablaze with fiery, ruddy light, as if the nearby city were burning. Beware, says Vengeance-in-Silver, for it's an echo of the old revolutions and violence of the city, and danger abounds on those nights. Look for opportunity, says the Eaten Wolf, for the one who braves the flames and draws from the banquet beyond returns with a belly full of secrets. Watch for these apparitions of fiery night, says the Fishing Cat, for they are bleed-offs of the massive spiritual energies flowing into the Zero Point and indicate stresses and weak spots on the cromlech lines. <br /> Those cromlech lines are ancient routes of spiritual power that run into the city from all manner of direction, lining up with the cromlechs of past eras in a vast grid of energy. This grid, says the Fishing Cat, is what ties Paris into the wider France as its symbolic heart, and what makes events in Paris so important to the rest of the country. The problem is that, in recent decades, possibly since the Dance of the Lights in the 1960's, the power is surging inwards uncontrollably and throwing all things out of balance. The lines come together at the Zero Point of Paris, by Notre Dame. Handling this overload is the proclaimed purpose of the Zero Point Protectorate, but the spiritual lines can have strange effects on all the territories they run through. The Eaten Wolf says that they're lines of the dead, that the cromlech are linked to the groaning grave-sites buried beneath Paris. The Fishing Cat says that one of the cromlech lines runs under Montreuil as it passes towards the Zero Point.<br /> <br /> It is the tradition of Parisian Uratha that the resting places of noted werewolves are sacred locations, especially to the Hunters in Darkness and Bone Shadows. The proper reverence and maintenance of such sites is considered <i>right behaviour</i>, itself a measure of honour. Those who disdain their forebears and the noble dead are living only in the moment and insulting the history of the Forsaken. The Eaten Wolf mutters about tombs as wells and sinkholes that suck down Death essence; the Fishing Cat firmly instructs that honouring the past is paramount; Vengeance-in-Silver leaves no doubt that handling such sites will affect how both spirits <i>and</i> Uratha look upon the pack.<br /> <br /> The Sacre Coeur in Monmartre is sacred to both Forsaken and Pure, a place of penance and neutral ground. The humans raised up the cathedral there as a symbol of order and spirituality that would reimpose old cultural strictures upon France; it is akin to both an immense lightning rod and attennae at the same time, its structure plugging into the <i>immense</i> Locus that swirls and seethes beneath it. Its architect, and many of his leading workers, became Claimed by <i>something</i> during the construction, leading to a bloody purge by the Uratha in 1914. Even the Eaten Wolf just shakes her head when speaking of the Sacred Heart, simply advising that it is consecrated with blood and should not be disrespected.<br /> <br /> Oh, and don't mess with the cats in the Monmartre graveyards. Just don't.<br /> <b>The Uratha of Paris</b><br /> The Forsaken of Paris are broadly split between the Lamplighters Protectorate that holds wide swathes of territory in the banlieues, the Zero Point Protectorate that struggles to keep its grip in the arrondisements, and those packs that remain unaffiliated with either. There are a great number of Uratha in Paris, more than one might expect, and still there is much unclaimed space to be taken by newcomers.<br /> <br /> The Zero Point Protectorate formed back in the early 90s among the packs of the central arrondissements, in response to the discovery of the growing energies in the cromlech lines by the Bone Shadows of the Red Children pack. The overall purpose of the Protectorate is to monitor the cromlech lines, prevent a disastrous level of Essence forming in the zero point itself, and to do what they can to discover what is causing the problem and to prevent any other creatures from using or aggravating the surge. Because the Protectorate's territories include various symbols that are important to the wider Shadow of France, they have good connections and influence with Uratha from beyond Paris, and hold many valuable spiritual resources. However, the Protectorate's creation caused plenty of friction. The Protectorate of the Dance, formed in the 60s, was slowly falling apart by the end of the 80s and the formation of the Zero Point Protectorate caused it to topple; the new, more insular Protectorate cut many of the Uratha of Paris out from the influence and access they had once enjoyed.<br /> <br /> The Lamplighters Protectorate formed around ten years ago, binding together the more powerful packs of the banlieues under the leadership of two elders - the ancient Blood Talon Scourge-of-Valais and the Iron Master Dolon Laguerre. The two elders are reputed to loathe one another, but the collapse of the Protectorate of the Dance had left both of them with greatly weakened power-bases. Fortunately for them, they were able to take advantage of the Zero Point's focus on the cromlech lines and the spiritual energies within the Isle-de-France itself, a focus that left fewer resources and less aid being given to the packs out in the banlieues. During a renewed period of Pure aggression, one that scattered two packs entirely, the elders managed to put aside their differences and forge the Lamplighters under the banner of fighting the war and shouldering the duties to the Forsaken that Zero Point seemed unwilling to do. More numerous than Zero Point but more widely scattered and less well-resourced, the Lamplighters have nonetheless managed to fight back effectively against the Pure and take some steps to managing the rest of the city's unstable spiritual ecology. The two ravenous elders, however, are as much feared as they are respected, and often refered to mockingly as Hirsent and Isengrim when out of earshot.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves are extremely numerous in Paris, largely as very small packs or even individuals in the banlieues. Many have a warped mixture of Uratha and Christian (or Muslim) beliefs; these werewolves are usually referred to as devil dogs or hellhounds by other Uratha, since they tend to believe that they are demons or have been cursed by Satan in some way. A few maintain cults of Ys, maintaining a myth of the sunken city that considers it as both lost homeland and promised paradise that they can attain by through hunting whoever it is that their particular cult holds as sacred prey; both the Storm Lords and the Fire-Touched use the Ys cults as intermediary recruiting grounds, the latter as a step towards the belief of Taga Dan. Unfortunately, lone Ghost Wolves also often seem to form their own little cults of humans in France, teaching rite-craft to the herd and preparing cultists to become Claimed for their spirit-allies; these cults have been a major source of witches and sorcerers over the centuries, but at least in Paris they used to be easier to hunt down. The vast population of the city now means the opposite is true; it's easy for a cult to hide amongst the masses.<br /> <br /> The Apollonians are a source of trouble for the Zero Point Protectorate in particular, and contest a few key territories in the arrondissements and inner banlieues. These bizarre cultists are all members of an esoteric lodge of Uratha who worship Apollo in his aspect as a wolf, and reject the Forsaken and Pure mythologies alike. They consider themselves to be guardians of places that are sacred to the Light of the Sun, and the Forsaken have some evidence that they may have started as a Hunter in Darkness heresy. The Apollonians have been practicing their frenzied, ecstatic rites and debauched entertainments for at least a couple of centuries. The lodge <i>claims</i> to hold defilers of their sacred places as their holy prey, but the hidden little shrines can hardly have enough curious trespassers to justify the Apollonian cult's numbers.<br /> <br /> The Amazigh are traditionalist Uratha from the Berber immigrants into France, both Pure and Forsaken alike. Amazigh packs are insular and refuse to embrace any werewolves who are not strict adherents to the supposed traditions of the Maghreb Uratha, even other immigrants who they judge to not hold to the old ways enough. The Amazigh hold themselves to be purer and wiser than French Uratha, regardless of those Urathas' origins, and while they do partake in the Forsaken Protectorates and the Pure cults, they always hold themselves aloof to some extent. Even the rivalries and feuds amongst the Amazigh Pure and Forsaken are highly opaque to outsiders. The Amazigh lack numbers, however, and their power is only likely to diminish and take them closer to irrelevance as even young Berber-immigrant Uratha feel they have little in common with some traditionalists following old and strict rites for little obvious practical benefit.<br /> <br /> As for the Pure? Well, they have their own divisions and rifts. The Ivory Claws of the Silver Principality, centred in Versailles, are united but their influence in Paris itself is strictly limited. The rival Fire-Touched sects of the Iron Banner, the Blind Sight and the Scarlet Cathedral squabble with each other and the other Tribes for power. Old families of Ivory Claw lineage sneer at the Fire-Touched masses but carefully trade their knowledge and skills to Rabid Wolf's children in return for the lore and the blood that they seek. Even their totems are divided, and not along Tribal lines; a small enclave of Fire-Touched in the far west recently came under attack by both Fire-Touched and Predator King packs, whose totems sought the destruction of the enclave's own spirits due to some transgression or other.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Territory - Montreuil</span></b><br /> At the beginning of the Chronicle, the pack's territory is however much of the banlieue of Montreuil that they want to try and claim. Montreuil is a poor banlieue, and has major problems with drug-related crime. Nearly a tenth of it is simply deserted - an urban playground of crumbling blocks of flats, dilapidated industrial warehouses and rusting factories. The entire place is an utter patchwork of different eras of construction, old buildings and new concrete horrors jostling with one another. There are even old, 19th Century mansions. The bones of Montreuil's past push up through its fabric.<br /> <br /> Although decrepit and run-down, there is an atmosphere of hope in Montreuil. Many young workers are being attracted to the area due to the very low rents, and some have even taken to calling it the '21st arrondissement' in a fit of excessive optimism. Some Uratha have noticed there now seem to be very few old people in Montreuil at all - <i>oddly</i> few. Since the 80s there has been a steady influx of artists and intellectuals, a thriving creative community with a halo of drug dealers, mad spirits and surprising inspiration nestled amongst artists' squats. Old film-making studios, some of the first to ever be established, still tie Montreuil with strong symbolic links to the concepts of illusion and the unreal.<br /> <br /> Local government is controlling and bureaucratic. They wrap local organisations in red tape if they don't play ball, and have little tolerance for beggars, Roma and other 'undesirables'. There is also a strong push in the administration for the suppression of cults, and considerable antipathy towards Islamic practices. Ethnic tensions are a problem, exacerbated by poverty. Montreuil has a particularly large immigrant community from Mali, but it doesn't seem to currently include any Uratha.<br /> <br /> <b>Past Uratha of Montreuil</b><br /> The history of Montreuil's former packs, at least in as much as the pack have been given bits and pieces of it, falls roughly thus.<br /> <br /> Montreuil has had its Uratha guardians over the centuries. Back in the late 17th Century, when Montreuil was mostly groves of peach trees, one Bishop Guillaume (called 'the Wolf' by his human ecclesiastical contemporaries for his predatory aspect and intimidating manner) levered his influence to great effect against the growing influence of the Ivory Claws that accompanied the construction of the Versailles palace-complex. Still remembered by modern Uratha, the Iron Master is considered a paragon of both Cunning and Honour.<br /> <br /> At some point in the early 20th Century, Montreuil became the territory of a pack called the White Masques who held it over subsequent generations. This ended in the 60s during what the older Uratha have variously called the Turning of the Circle, the Swirling War or the Dance of the Lights. Widespread spiritual disruption accompanied the movement or disruption of the city's foci of spiritual power, resulting in packs desperately struggling over a suddenly shifting landscape of resources. The White Masques collapsed during the strife, with many dying and others moving on to new territory and new packs.<br /> <br /> The territory was then unclaimed for about a decade or so, until in the late 70s a predominantly Ghost Wolf pack moved into the area and attempted to hold it. This pack, the Mirrors, clung on until the 90s when internal struggles and conflict with the Pure caused them to disband and move on. Since then, singular Ghost Wolves have sometimes tried to claim turf in the banlieue but have never stayed for long.<br /> <br /> This changed a few years ago. A Ghost Wolf called the Changeling, going by the name of Louis Moreau, established a cult in the banlieue. Hidden from the gaze of Blood Talon and Iron Master witch-hunters, the Changeling created the New Association of Illuminated Thought, a supposed self-help/New Age spiritual group known to the inner circles as the Transmutative Path. The Path's philosophy was one of self-change at a powerful, spiritual level - cult members believed that they would be fundamentally changed as they were immersed in the mysteries, gaining enlightenment and a release from the needs of the material world. This was literally true - the Changeling selected promising candidates for Claiming to be promoted to the innermost ranks of the Path, offering the flesh-shells to the spirits of hope, despair and madness that thronged around him. Other cultists 'disappeared' to far-off training courses or 'left the faith' - in fact consumed by the Changeling and his Claimed for the bounty of Essence in their meat. By harnessing the cultists as his pack, the Changeling was also able to work strange rites over them, further strengthening his influence. When the local government flagged the NAIT as a cult, finally bringing the attention of watchful Iron Masters and Storm Lords to bear, Written-in-Blood's former life was already entangled in the cult, resulting in the explosive showdown that began the Changeling's defeat. While the cult was torn down by the combined efforts of the newly formed pack, the Changeling itself escaped to destinations unknown.<br /> <br /> <b>The Base of Operations</b><br /> The pack holds as their base the former junkyard, now sculptor's trove, that Howling Phantom's family money acquired. Within the junkyard is a relaltively potent Locus of Metal, born from years of iron and steel being crushed and smashed and left to rust, and from older traces of fire and bronze. The junkyard has several buildings and sheds within it, relatively high walls with barbed wire at their height, and grounds that are well concealed from neighbouring buildings.<br /> <br /> Across the road from the junkyard are the last crumbling ruins of a very old bronze foundry. Part of the foundry actually ran under where the junkyard now stands, but the skeleton of the rest of the building remains a haunting reminder of the region's industrial past. This foundry is the home of the totem spirit, the last vestiges of its own former reflection; the Enduring Smith has only survived this long through drinking from the Locus of Metal to sustain itself, and it is now a clattering thing of verdigris, rust and dying embers rather than its former glories of gleaming bronze.<br /> <br /> The former cultists of the Transmutative Path who have now joined the pack's ranks live in their own homes scattered around the banlieue. Some are very remote, coming together with the rest of the pack only on those specific nights when a fire is lit out in the junkyard and they come to find comradeship with their fellow survivors; but even these packmates always keep their eyes open, make sure to send emails or texts in for anything suspicious that they encounter, and ensure that their trades and places of work offer pack members good prices and favourable opportunities. The other pack-mates are more dedicated to the here and now, throwing themselves into pack work with enthusiasm or desperation - helping guard the junkyard, actively patrolling the streets, watching for changes in the graffiti and the gangs or even trying to worm their way deeper into the occult community of Paris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T14:21:01-08:00","id":393031,"title":"","content":"You'll note that there's not much info about the Tribes in there. That's partly because the players have read the new Tribe briefs, partly because they're playing very new Uratha whose backstories generally gave them very strong reasons to join their particular Tribes, and partly because I'm still working on what Lodges etc should be present amongst the Tribes (the Blood Talons, for example, have numerous of the Lodge of Garm present, but rather than the Lodge of Wendigo they instead have the Matagots, who follow a similar general philosophy but tied instead to more local myths and folklore).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T16:49:40-08:00","id":394283,"title":"","content":"And there's our first session successfully completed! No-one died either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, none of the player characters, anyway.<br /> <br /> A good game. Social Facets were appropriately used to get what the characters wanted and handle a Wolf-Blooded with anger issues who was on drugs, and the characters encountered three of the High Cromlech's Claimed servants - each possessed by a Rank 2 spirit. Despite the Claimed making an attempt to parlay for what they wanted, it ended in a fight, one where the three Claimed managed to cause horrific damage until the werewolves in the pack busted out Gauru.<br /> <br /> I am definitely very happy with just how horrific the final version of Gauru has ended up being.<br /> <br /> Hopefully next time the pack will be able to wrap up locating the bones of an Uratha from the 60s, recruit the somewhat mad Wolf-Blooded to their pack, then set to exerting their control across their wider territory and starting to try to get a grip on the spirit ecology of Montreuil. From what they've seen so far when peering across the Gauntlet, it's not gonna be easy...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T17:58:59-08:00","id":394306,"title":"","content":"How long was the session both in-game and out of game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T18:32:18-08:00","id":394339,"title":"","content":"Wow it took me a while to get through the write-up but it's fantastic.<br /> <br /> I particularly like the mentors and tutors, were they created with the players, or by them or what?<br /> <br /> And the Past Uratha section is a good idea, we'll have to do something like that. I like the Changeling, too, to be honest I kept thinking about that when playing Werewolf. If you found someone you could justify giving to a spirit you knew, would you be able to leverage that into getting a Claimed ally? It was just something interesting to ponder over. I like the heavy religious bent everything's tinged with, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T21:09:26-08:00","id":394420,"title":"","content":"Here's an old story seed I was playing around with for a game that never happened. Figured it might fit in with Paris considering the popular notion of French cuisine being very fancy and including many exotic dishes (particularly if you're not French yourself)<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> There's a restaurant the locals almost never go to. Which is odd because it's in a fairly nice location and the food is delicious. The restaurant makes most its business off of tourists out for the night to try the exotic French cuisine. They all leave as satisfied customers.<br /> But if you dine there more than a few times something starts to feel....off about the place. You can't put your finger on it but there's something disturbing in the atmosphere. So the locals have learnt to stay clear. And for good reason.<br /> <br /> The head chef was once a mediocre cook. Not awful but also not the genius he desperately wanted to be. Then he attracted the attention of a spirit of Creativity. Drawn to the chef's ambition for creating new exciting dishes the spirit decided to lend a helping hand. It didn't take long for the chef to become Ridden.<br /> It was innocent at first. The spirit urged the chef to try some new recipes he'd never thought of before and suddenly his cooking was a great success. Basking in the glory of his newfound skill the chef couldn't be happier. But the spirit wanted more, always more. And the chef found himself trying some...unusual ingredients. Some pets and stray animals disappeared, no big deal. But the spirit continued to urge the chef to find ever more exotic ingredients, so as to create even more exciting dishes. Maybe a few tourists disappeared. No matter, the new meat dish was extraordinary. Even got a mention in some nice reviews.<br /> <br /> It's still not enough. Now the spirit of Creativity (having Claimed the chef completely) is looking for even more rare ingredients. And it's looking among the denizens of the World of Darkness. A Changeling's body was transformed by it's time in Arcadia. What flavors might it yield? Does a Beshilu taste better than a regular rat? Can such a thing even be turned into a gourmet dish? What kind of food can be made from the even rarer, one of a kind, creatures one sometimes come across in the dark corners of Paris?<br /> <br /> Even better, the Creativity spirit's latest experiments involve using other spirits in it's cooking. Through rare Numina it has learnt how to bind spirits of different kinds into it's dishes as a form of ephemeral seasoning in the hopes of elevating the dining experience. The Creativity spirit has even gone so far as to capture some spirits and fatten them up by force feeding them with spirits of widely different choirs, creating strange and twisted Magath. The spirit of Creativity hope that these different combinations will let it find the perfect spiritual &quot;flavor&quot;.<br /> <br /> What could happen to a normal human eating these strange, exotic dishes? Nothing good, most likely, particularly since the spirits consumed with the food tend to stay with the patrons long after they've left the restaurant.<br /> The Creativity spirit's influence has begun to spread and smaller spirits of similar nature has latched on and begun to Urge or Claim the rest of the restaurant's staff. Anyone trying to stop them would be in for a handful.<br /> Still it's only a matter of time until this comes to the attention of a pack of Uratha. The Creativity spirit has only become more and more brazen in it's hunt for new ingredients.<br /> <br /> Recently it has even occurred to the spirit what wonderful flavors one might be able to coax from the flesh of a Werewolf!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","user":"baboonking","date":". 02-06-2015, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T05:49:12-08:00","id":394706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=394306#post394306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long was the session both in-game and out of game?</div> </div> </div> </div>The game ran about 3 hours as we started later than usual (usually approx 4 hours), albeit with a roughly 15 minute break in the middle.<br /> <br /> When we can start podcasting you'll be able to hear for yourself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In-game, much less time because there was a) a combat and b) a lot of description, people getting a feel for their characters, rechecking rules as we familiarise ourselves with the post-playtest changes, etc. Roughly 4 scenes - observing a building and planning the entry, the initial exploration within and encountering some residents, finding the Wolf-Blooded and having to talk him down and deal with the aftermath, and finally hunting down the Claimed to first try and negotiate with them and then breaking out into combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=394339#post394339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow it took me a while to get through the write-up but it's fantastic.<br /> <br /> I particularly like the mentors and tutors, were they created with the players, or by them or what?<br /> <br /> And the Past Uratha section is a good idea, we'll have to do something like that. I like the Changeling, too, to be honest I kept thinking about that when playing Werewolf. If you found someone you could justify giving to a spirit you knew, would you be able to leverage that into getting a Claimed ally? It was just something interesting to ponder over. I like the heavy religious bent everything's tinged with, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Howling and Written don't have any mentor dots, so I just wrote their tutors up as I wanted. Bianca has 4 dots in Mentor and gave me the initial idea of who she wanted her Mentor to be (an older relative and significant figure in the city) so I worked from that as a starting point (as a note, the Street of the Fishing Cat is a real place). Everyone was happy with the result, but had there been any major issues I would have just reworked the tutors as desired.<br /> <br /> As for the Claimed, yep, the Changeling's cult is basically a nasty mirror of a regular Werewolf pack, bringing Claimed into the structure and treating the human tier as a resource rather than as people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baboonking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=394420#post394420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an old story seed I was playing around with for a game that never happened. Figured it might fit in with Paris considering the popular notion of French cuisine being very fancy and including many exotic dishes (particularly if you're not French yourself)<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting story seed, I may well make use of it in some form in the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:29:08-08:00","id":394998,"title":"","content":"I'm loving your write ups here Acro. Reading how you prepare the setting details and chronicle information is going to help me a lot when I start up my own chronicle I'll be starting down the line when one of my friends conclude one of their games. Organizing thoughts and themes and such has always been one of my greater challenges when GMing, leading me to lean on improvisation a lot more than I would like in my previous games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T15:26:20-08:00","id":395503,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering!<br /> <br /> I'm also curious how many Beats were given out in this session, and how many of those were from fulfilling Aspirations vs other sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T17:19:29-08:00","id":395655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=394998#post394998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving your write ups here Acro. Reading how you prepare the setting details and chronicle information is going to help me a lot when I start up my own chronicle I'll be starting down the line when one of my friends conclude one of their games. Organizing thoughts and themes and such has always been one of my greater challenges when GMing, leading me to lean on improvisation a lot more than I would like in my previous games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! If you have any questions then let me know, subject of course to 2e-specific stuff having to wait for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=395503#post395503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answering!<br /> <br /> I'm also curious how many Beats were given out in this session, and how many of those were from fulfilling Aspirations vs other sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>20 Beats in total were earned. We're using the Group Beats optional rule.<br /> <br /> Started with 4 Beats base, one per player as the 'participation' Beat. Then I threw in 5 additional Beats at the end for general story progress etc (it wasn't necessarily going to be 5 specifically but we were at 15 at that point so it felt nice to end the first session with everyone getting an Experience). Of the remaining 11, I think... 4 or 5 were tagged from Aspirations? The rest were a mixture of Conditions resolving (all gained by exceptional successes) and bonus Beats based off stuff happening in game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:30:00-08:00","id":411592,"title":"","content":"Our next session is tonight!<br /> <br /> I'm currently statting out the idigam (not expecting to need the stats any time soon, but it helps with filling out their characters in the setting), figuring out how the <i>Ukusgualu</i><i>, </i>the Lamprey Hosts, work, and filling out the roster of packs, spirit courts, cults and factions. There are weird entities like the Chancel, ancient and dusty undying who watch the deathly aspect of the city with interest; the Drinkers of the Well, a mad cult of Uratha who worship something that is basically a snail-shoggoth, and an entire drug-running gang run by Azlu.<br /> <br /> It's also time to fill out more ideas for what's in the territory, as the characters will have the chance to start setting their own agenda and figuring out what they want to do to their turf tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:55:58-08:00","id":412041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=411592#post411592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and an entire drug-running gang run by Azlu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since watching Dredd, I wanted to make a powerful Azlu based off of Ma-Ma sitting at the top of a housing project, running her web of criminals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T06:08:02-08:00","id":415076,"title":"","content":"Our second session went well! Weird entities, strange phone calls (including from the data idigam!), sorting the pack name out and ritually claiming their territory. The Bone Shadow is carefully keeping track of every slight that a spirit gives him for later retribution, while still dealing with them for the time being. The Storm Lord is carefully making a list of Things To Do in sorting their territory out. The Blood Talon is providing the blunt voice of practicality, as only a person with Intelligence 1 can do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Wolf-Blooded is planning on how to get the equipment he needs to start making bronze arrowheads, because that will please the totem.<br /> <br /> The totem's just being weird, including scaring the fuck out of one of the human pack members who was going to take out some rubbish that included (gasp) reusable metal in it. Sacrelige!<br /> <br /> So they've made their mark on the banlieue, to the point where their ritual claiming of the territory involved spraying over the gang graffiti tags with their own and even roughing up some of the drug dealers etc they met. This caused a retaliatory graffiti attack on the pack's home, the junkyard. This in turn caused them to go and find the gang members responsible, resulting in them breaking into the drug den, resulting in one gang member trying to do a runner out of a window and onto the rooftop, <i>resulting in</i> the Wolf-Blooded and his Parkour merit going after them, <i>resulting in</i> a rooftop chase that didn't get very far before the gang member slipped and nearly fell off the roof, saved only from a messy death by a lucky roll from the Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Wolf-Blooded also identified Hunter marks amongst the graffiti sprayed on the junkyard, but he doesn't recognise what organisation they're from. He also has absolutely abysmal social skills and hence utterly fluffed his attempt to poke his Hunter contacts for info. Back when he worked for the Office, there were research teams to do that sort of thing for him. Not any more :P<br /> <br /> Another pack's Elodoth also spent some time laying into him for being a weak link in the pack and untrustworthy, then spent time laying into the rest of the pack for the fact they'd let her chew out one of their pack members without leaping to his defence.<br /> <br /> Anyway, fun times. Ancient dust-breathing women who claim to be part of something called 'The Chancel', a phone call from a being calling itself The Operator that quite happily gave them one free answer to any question in celebration of their pack's formation, and a belligerent road-car-spider-thing spirit that gave the Ithaeur all sorts of info about the local spirit politics in return for that tasty, tasty Essence. And now it knows there's a locus on the pack's turf, and is going to go tell that to its 'boss', the spirit noble of pollution and decay that's a middle-manager in an even bigger spirit of urban decay's court.<br /> <br /> At some point I'll introduce the Ghost Wolf who's infected with Lamprey Hosts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=412041#post412041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever since watching Dredd, I wanted to make a powerful Azlu based off of Ma-Ma sitting at the top of a housing project, running her web of criminals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T07:41:50-08:00","id":415134,"title":"","content":"Your game is just an amazing thing to read. I particularly like how everyone is getting so into their tribal oaths, and into marking their territories. What happened to the rest of the gang they hunted down besides the one who did a runner?<br /> <br /> Also, how does your Blood Talon player portray a character with Intelligence 1? Are we talking someone with mental disabilities, or just someone who is thoroughly uneducated and uninterested in intellectual pursuits besides?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-22-2015, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:14:41-08:00","id":415592,"title":"","content":"My changeling had an intelligence of 1, it was surprisingly fun, though I ended up having to roll whenever he used his smartphone. He was more of a himbo at the start, though.<br /> <br /> What did the werewolves do when they busted into the drug den? Threaten them into moving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:24:04-08:00","id":416349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=415134#post415134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your game is just an amazing thing to read. I particularly like how everyone is getting so into their tribal oaths, and into marking their territories. What happened to the rest of the gang they hunted down besides the one who did a runner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they were expecting there to be 3-5 people in the gang but, of course, at the time they broke in there were only two there. The poor sod watching tv downstairs got jumped from behind by the Bone Shadow in Dalu and grappled into submission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how does your Blood Talon player portray a character with Intelligence 1? Are we talking someone with mental disabilities, or just someone who is thoroughly uneducated and uninterested in intellectual pursuits besides? </div> </div> </div>Poorly educated, never really paid much attention in school, has lived a life prior to the First Change drifting from one manual labour job to another, never had any intellectual aspirations. The player keeps reminding himself that his character just doesn't really know very much about non-practical stuff, so doesn't pick up on various bits of interesting information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=415592#post415592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My changeling had an intelligence of 1, it was surprisingly fun, though I ended up having to roll whenever he used his smartphone. He was more of a himbo at the start, though.<br /> <br /> What did the werewolves do when they busted into the drug den? Threaten them into moving?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters they made their move in the middle of the day for some reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Admittedly it's a really crappy area of town, but still... Anyway, the pack circled the building; the Irraka went round the back and came crashing through a ground floor window when the rest of the pack slammed through the front door. They quickly subdued one gang member but the other one fled after a failed ambush with a baseball bat at the top of the stairs, and thence to rooftop chases <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No chance yet to even threaten them into moving, we ended the session with the runner being subdued <i>and</i> saved from falling to his death by the Wolf-Blooded pretty much dislocating his shoulder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:04:46-08:00","id":419571,"title":"","content":"I am curious: roughly how many werewolves do you think there are in your Paris?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T06:59:30-08:00","id":420114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=419571#post419571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious: roughly how many werewolves do you think there are in your Paris?</div> </div> </div> </div>A shit-load. In my game, France specifically has an unusually high number of werewolves (for reasons that I will explain when the 2e corebook comes out - sorry to keep saying that, but I don't want to spoil any more of the book as we edge ever closer to release!).<br /> <br /> Scarily, if you go by the 'nearly half a million Uratha in the world' stat that turned up somewhere in first edition, that would mean the urban area of Paris has <i>hundreds</i> of werewolves in it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:20:49-08:00","id":420946,"title":"","content":"This lack of Werewolf 2e is driving me into despair! Next month, right? RIGHT?<br /> <br /> Hundreds of werewolves all in one place is a disturbing idea. Which means I really, really like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:20:44-08:00","id":420986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=420946#post420946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This lack of Werewolf 2e is driving me into despair! Next month, right? RIGHT?</div> </div> </div> </div>I;m saying this to myself from October... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=420946#post420946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hundreds of werewolves all in one place is a disturbing idea. Which means I really, really like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, it got me thinking about first <i>Underworld </i>movie... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/MqT-e44kIM8\" data-code=\"MqT-e44kIM8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/MqT-e44kIM8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T07:36:53-08:00","id":421742,"title":"","content":"Yeah this is probably the longest I've gone without gaming in ten years. I keep thinking to do just a short game but don't want to start it up then cut it off if Idigam Chronicles comes out in a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:37:49-08:00","id":422303,"title":"","content":"Today's game, while a day late due to toddler issues yesterday, was very good.<br /> <br /> The pack have roughed up drug dealers, been given some 'helpful' information by an Amazigh Ivory Claw (who really disapproves of a criminal organisation they are clashing with because Magrebhi and white French mix in its ranks! Gasp!), encountered a poor bastard Ghost Wolf trying to nab Essence from their Locus who is infested with <i>Ukusgualu</i><i>,</i> met an actual <i>Ukusgualu</i> and <i>probably</i> killed it, and ended up with the Ghost Wolf strapped to a medical table in a criminal back street surgery, slicing him open to yank the writhing lampreys out from his guts. The Ghost Wolf, who has <i>wildly</i> imbalanced Harmony, managed to pass double figures of Death Rage checks despite having a Willpower dice pool of 4! They also did their first proper Sacred Hunt rite (targeting the Ghost Wolf) and used the new tracking rules to great effect (when trying to track the Ghost Wolf down to his riverside lair).<br /> <br /> End result of all that included a pretty massive pile of Beats - 29 in the pot from this session. Everyone's now earned 3 Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:35:28-08:00","id":422386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=422303#post422303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today's game, while a day late due to toddler issues yesterday, was very good.<br /> <br /> The pack have roughed up drug dealers, been given some 'helpful' information by an Amazigh Ivory Claw (who really disapproves of a criminal organisation they are clashing with because Magrebhi and white French mix in its ranks! Gasp!), encountered a poor bastard Ghost Wolf trying to nab Essence from their Locus who is infested with <i>Ukusgualu</i><i>,</i> met an actual <i>Ukusgualu</i> and <i>probably</i> killed it, and ended up with the Ghost Wolf strapped to a medical table in a criminal back street surgery, slicing him open to yank the writhing lampreys out from his guts. The Ghost Wolf, who has <i>wildly</i> imbalanced Harmony, managed to pass double figures of Death Rage checks despite having a Willpower dice pool of 4! They also did their first proper Sacred Hunt rite (targeting the Ghost Wolf) and used the new tracking rules to great effect (when trying to track the Ghost Wolf down to his riverside lair).<br /> <br /> End result of all that included a pretty massive pile of Beats - 29 in the pot from this session. Everyone's now earned 3 Experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From this, I learned that the Sacred Hunt don't necessarily need a death at the end of the hunt...<br /> <br /> This opens up very interesting possibilities in my head right now. Not sure why I was thinking that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T03:58:49-08:00","id":422797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=422386#post422386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> From this, I learned that the Sacred Hunt don't necessarily need a death at the end of the hunt...<br /> <br /> This opens up very interesting possibilities in my head right now. Not sure why I was thinking that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed not. Bringing down the prey doesn't necessarily mean killing them and, in certain very specific metaphorical circumstances might involve no physical violence at all.<br /> <br /> In this case, when they found their prey he was kinda... pre-downed on account of being asleep and then, when he woke, was surrounded by the pack :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:40:49-08:00","id":422905,"title":"","content":"I think I'm also going to need to come up with a standard shortlist of off-the-cuff Conditions to grant from exceptional successes at perception rolls.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are <i>very</i> good at perception rolls. None of my lot even have Trained Observer or the appropriate Wolf Gift for a boost either, and exceptional successes are already fairly common, as these things go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:40:19-08:00","id":423412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=422905#post422905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm also going to need to come up with a standard shortlist of off-the-cuff Conditions to grant from exceptional successes at perception rolls.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are <i>very</i> good at perception rolls. None of my lot even have Trained Observer or the appropriate Wolf Gift for a boost either, and exceptional successes are already fairly common, as these things go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Intended? Or unexpected side effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:44:17-08:00","id":423413,"title":"","content":"What forms do you find that your players tend to use most often so far? How often do they tend to change shapes?<br /> <br /> Have any of them had any Harmony Breaking Points so far? If so, do they tend to get more Flesh or more Spirit ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T05:58:45-08:00","id":424037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=423412#post423412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Intended? Or unexpected side effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's intended. I was hoping we'd find space in the senses section of the book to add in some pre-done Perception Exceptional Success Conditions on precisely the basis that I expected there to be a lot of them for werewolf characters, but I don't think there was the wordcount in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=423413#post423413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What forms do you find that your players tend to use most often so far? How often do they tend to change shapes?<br /> <br /> Have any of them had any Harmony Breaking Points so far? If so, do they tend to get more Flesh or more Spirit ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forms are a real mixture, to be honest. A lot of Dalu and Urhan because they're in a city, but Urshul when things look fighty and Gauru when, well you know when Gauru is necessary.<br /> <br /> Notable that the Irraka tore a massive hole in a Ghost Wolf with Eviscerate while just in Urhan form, though, with a hit for something like 8 lethal.<br /> <br /> Shapechanging is very, very frequent.<br /> <br /> Harmony Breaking Points - yes, and an Integrity breaking point for the Wolf-Blooded, but no-one's failed so far. We nearly had one last session when the players <i>could</i> have killed the infested Ghost Wolf (and at one point nearly did so accidentally, just due to the above Irraka's ambush hitting <i>so</i> hard) but they didn't in the end. Have a few more Breaking Points planned along the way just as the pack settle into their more werewolf-y lives, as well as obviously anything they specifically do that triggers one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:00:49-08:00","id":424038,"title":"","content":"Oh, and on the forms, regular Hishu is obviously used a lot of the time, but not just because it's seen as the 'default' - Hishu does have its own advantages now, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:07:48-08:00","id":424102,"title":"","content":"Yes, speaking of blending in: How have you handled the fact that Urhan are wolves, and wolves are not generally a sight you see in a city? Do people take notice of this, or...? How's that working out for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:16:21-08:00","id":424122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=424102#post424102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, speaking of blending in: How have you handled the fact that Urhan are wolves, and wolves are not generally a sight you see in a city? Do people take notice of this, or...? How's that working out for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, they've been running with having a Hishu or human pack-member 'owner' with the Urhan 'dogs'. There are probably, what, 100 wolves in France total so 'obviously' the Urhan aren't actually wolves but just wolf-looking hounds. When they've had the Urhan split up while tracking, they've probably just been hoping that they'll get seen as feral dogs keeping to the back alleys etc.<br /> <br /> If they <i>keep</i> doing that, roving around in Urhan without an 'owner' with them, it may cause them problems. Lots of reports feral/ownerless dogs may get animal control paying attention - or even hapless animal charities who want to take the poor dogs into a shelter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It also makes it easier for other forces to detect the pack's activity, whether Uratha or other supernatural beings that are paying attention. Finally, should things go badly tits up and the area end up getting terrorised by the pack's antics and/or by the prey they're battling, the appearance of the wolves will likely feed into the general level of tension and fear amongst the regular population, which will further feed the fear Essence bleeding into the <i>Hisil</i> and may well give rise to wolf-like fear spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:25:18-08:00","id":424139,"title":"","content":"Wow, no wonder werewolves like rural territories so much. They don't usually have to worry about those concerns when roaming around in Urhan like they do in a city like Paris.<br /> <br /> Why did they feel the need to split up and take that risk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:44:02-08:00","id":424189,"title":"","content":"In prepping for my Detroit game, I've been reading up on coyotes. In the northeast U.S. and Canada, there has been a rise in &quot;coywolves&quot;, which are crossbreeds of coyotes, wolves, and dogs. They are larger than coyotes, hunt in packs, and are more aggressive and can take down larger prey. There was recently a news story about a woman with a farm near Detroit that raised horses for the police, who swears that a pack of large coyotes took down one of her animals. Given that my game is focused on one of the large urban prairies just east of Downtown Detroit, I intend to use this should the pack wander in Urhan. The coywolf thing is breaking news (a few recent articles on the web have brought it to public attention), so it would make sense for the media to latch onto any sighting to declare that coywolves are now hunting Detroit. Animal control response would give the Iron Masters things to deal with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:29:28-08:00","id":430248,"title":"","content":"We had our fourth session last night; a slightly slower Beat-count and broadly less <i>action</i> apart from a sudden fight with a spirit right at the very end. Still, there was some great roleplaying, internal tension and disputes over how to handle Gaspard the Ghost Wolf, the first flaring of Renown we've had. There was the moment where the ithaeur realised he might have <i>really</i> pissed off the pack totem who was, shall we say, less sedate and unemotional than they thought; the pack's first venture into the Shadow, when a garage-crab-trapdoor-spider thing tried to eat the Rahu once they'd gone so much as a few yards beyond the <i>Hisil</i> reflection of their junkyard; and more mundane concerns with gangs, turf and the ugly realities of a post-Charlie Hebdo shootings Paris.<br /> <br /> You can now, if you're so inclined, actually listen to the podcast of our first session over at <a href=\"https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/</a> where it's split into two parts. I think more will be going up over the next few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:10:16-08:00","id":430288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=424189#post424189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In prepping for my Detroit game, I've been reading up on coyotes. In the northeast U.S. and Canada, there has been a rise in &quot;coywolves&quot;, which are crossbreeds of coyotes, wolves, and dogs. They are larger than coyotes, hunt in packs, and are more aggressive and can take down larger prey. There was recently a news story about a woman with a farm near Detroit that raised horses for the police, who swears that a pack of large coyotes took down one of her animals. Given that my game is focused on one of the large urban prairies just east of Downtown Detroit, I intend to use this should the pack wander in Urhan. The coywolf thing is breaking news (a few recent articles on the web have brought it to public attention), so it would make sense for the media to latch onto any sighting to declare that coywolves are now hunting Detroit. Animal control response would give the Iron Masters things to deal with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Something else your Iron Masters might need to deal with, as a suggestion. Recently, the federal agency USPTO (United States Patent and Trademark Office) opened up satellite offices in a few locations around the nation and Detroit was the northern region picked. This might be of interest of Iron Masters as it could be a rush of spirits involved with Innovation, Ingenuity and Technology, but also spirits of Law and Oaths as well as spirits of Deception and related kin, likely in conflict with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:52:19-08:00","id":430351,"title":"","content":"These games sound great. I'll definitely be checking out that podcast, thank you for the link. Has anyone fulfilled a totem aspiration? It seems like an interesting addition.<br /> <br /> It might be ambitious to think our first game will be this weekend, but we've had the characters in mind for months now and we've already put on our finishing touches. I finally decided on elodoth, where before I was split on them and irraka. Both will be a first, as my own werewolf PCs tend to be shamans and NPCs tend more towards sages or warriors. There was pack of modern day pirates in our last game. I'm really liking Embodiment of the Firstborn, too, so I've used a chunk of my merits to grab it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:30:41-08:00","id":430386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=430351#post430351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These games sound great. I'll definitely be checking out that podcast, thank you for the link. Has anyone fulfilled a totem aspiration? It seems like an interesting addition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several people have hit the totem's aspiration I think, yes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we also have a bit of wiki up for the campaign now:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Werewolf_Paris\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Werewolf_Paris</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:51:46-07:00","id":434338,"title":"","content":"And session 2 is now up on the site as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm hoping the pack keep poking their noses around the Shadow at the beginning of session 5 rather than just retreating back into the Flesh; I plan a fairly large pitched fight against a whole load of opportunistic, hungry local spirits, both to test out the combat capability of the pack and to show them just how badly the Shadow needs wardens right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:25:34-07:00","id":436268,"title":"","content":"And the podcast of the third session is now up - this is the one with the Lamprey Host in it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> In Sanity We Trust Productions </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Regular RPG Podcast </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:22:53-07:00","id":437987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=424189#post424189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In prepping for my Detroit game, I've been reading up on coyotes. In the northeast U.S. and Canada, there has been a rise in &quot;coywolves&quot;, which are crossbreeds of coyotes, wolves, and dogs. They are larger than coyotes, hunt in packs, and are more aggressive and can take down larger prey. There was recently a news story about a woman with a farm near Detroit that raised horses for the police, who swears that a pack of large coyotes took down one of her animals. Given that my game is focused on one of the large urban prairies just east of Downtown Detroit, I intend to use this should the pack wander in Urhan. The coywolf thing is breaking news (a few recent articles on the web have brought it to public attention), so it would make sense for the media to latch onto any sighting to declare that coywolves are now hunting Detroit. Animal control response would give the Iron Masters things to deal with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I grew up in a farming community about an hour north of Detroit, Coyotes and Wolves ARE a serious issue all over the place even on the edges of larger towns and cities (coyotes not wolves). Good catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:42:56-07:00","id":438329,"title":"","content":"The podcast of the fourth session is now up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've also posted up the stats for the High Cromlech over in the New Idigam thread. Next up, the Operator, the 'data angel' <i>idigam</i> ensconced in La Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T15:54:36-07:00","id":466609,"title":"","content":"Finally got to have another session after several weeks with people on holiday and the like.<br /> <br /> Today's was a short one as we need to be up and off early tomorrow, but still was good. About half the session was spent on a large fight with spirits (something like 5 Rank 1 and 3 Rank 2 were involved during the course of the fight) and the rest dealing with the aftermath.<br /> <br /> I had fun with custom Numina, and I think it was generally a good example of how even lesser spirits can be a serious threat to werewolves. Also that the pack really need to turn themselves into a well-oiled hunting machine!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:13:44-07:00","id":466624,"title":"","content":"Can you let us know how ah, threatening they were? How did it go down?<br /> <br /> I would watch video, but it kills my bandwidth and I really am curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:22:45-07:00","id":466630,"title":"","content":"It's just sound, no video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:23:53-07:00","id":466633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=466630#post466630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just sound, no video.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Well, that certainly changes some things. How long do they tend to go on for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T16:37:06-07:00","id":466639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=466633#post466633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Well, that certainly changes some things. How long do they tend to go on for?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're divided into two parts, each part is usually like an hour or an hour and a half, one is just over two hours.<br /> <br /> I've heard people complain about podcasts where a small child makes an appearance, and apparently it is a dealbreaker for some. I've got a three year old so it's to be expected.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:01:54-07:00","id":467851,"title":"","content":"So, what did you do exactly to boost the Wolf-Blooded Hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:09:08-07:00","id":467858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=467851#post467851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what did you do exactly to boost the Wolf-Blooded Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>His wiki has the character sheet here: <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Werewolf_Paris/Henri\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Werewolf_Paris/Henri</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:27:56-07:00","id":467908,"title":"","content":"Oh cool, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:32:41-07:00","id":467954,"title":"","content":"Wow, yeah, Henri's pretty BA, the other werewolves aren't slouches either. My character feels suddenly inadequate with his one dot in Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T08:30:52-07:00","id":483550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=467851#post467851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what did you do exactly to boost the Wolf-Blooded Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Henri started with a big pool of bonus XP and has three Tells, not one.<br /> <br /> Just had our latest session last night; the pack have managed to poke the human fronts of a Fire-Touched pack that's pushing into their territory. Right now the Pures' totem, a Rank 3 spirit, is implacably pursuing one of the pack at roughly walking pace through Twilight.<br /> <br /> The pack are really quite shaken up about this - they know that the spirit is at <i>least</i> Rank 3 (due to the sheer penalty the spirit's Resistance put on an attempt to Shadow Gaze it), that it's probably seriously scary in combat and that it seems to have the Irraka's trail along with a considerable amount of determination to track her down. They're currently hoping that sunrise will lead to it calling off the hunt.<br /> <br /> They're going to be disappointed on that score <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The session also featured the Sinister Fire-Touched Freight Train, lots of crafting stuff, arguing about how to negotiate the local spiritual balance between light and dark, and some rather awkward interactions with Touchstones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T08:42:05-07:00","id":483568,"title":"","content":"Some of the custom Numina used by spirits so far:<br /> <br /> Howl of Despair - Power + Finesse opposed by Willpower (iirc) against one target, applies the Demoralized Condition if the target fails.<br /> <br /> High Impact - A ranged attack with Power + Finesse that inflicts a vehicle impact on the target.<br /> <br /> Maddening Ichors - Augments an attack by applying a spiritual drug to the victim, which I handled by rolling a die and counting down the list of drugs rules in the Bowery Dogs chapter of Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> Shredder - Augments an attack by adding a Tilt ala the Urshul benefit on it.<br /> <br /> Topple - A close area of effect attack that leaves the spirit without Defence for a turn afterwards (this is what the building spirit did when it 'fell' on the fight).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:42:55-07:00","id":483669,"title":"","content":"Dang! What kind of Spirit is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:06:36-07:00","id":498974,"title":"","content":"The spirit chasing the pack, the Hewn, is quite a specific spirit - that of stone that has been carven into images of worship and reverence. It's one of an entire brood of such spirits that are ruling over a particular Fire-Touched sect of packs, each wrought from the frenzied emotions, human misery and religious ecstasy surrounding particular crafted works.<br /> <br /> As of two sessions later, the pack are still all alive, so that's something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They've now actually made a big list of all the things they need to sort out, debts they need to repay, enemies they need to take out and tasks they have to accomplish soon, and are systematically working through it. They're currently sorting out the really immediate stuff - repaying some debts and hunting down certain foes - and are also working hard to gather some spiritual allies and prepare for the big decision - which of the two Forsaken Protectorates in Paris they should align themselves with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:32:17-07:00","id":508883,"title":"","content":"And there we go, Episode 6 is now up on <a href=\"https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://insanitywetrust.wordpress.com/</a> - only 2 episodes behind now, although it'll be three again after this evening's game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T07:34:56-07:00","id":510639,"title":"","content":"And Episode 7 is up now too!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A tangential thought about stories in nWoD:<br /> <br /> So one of the structural elements of the nWoD system is the 'story', a particular story arc that has mechanical impact as a concept. For example, Auspice Abilities are useable once per story.<br /> <br /> Sometimes when running games, I keep to tight arcs that work well with this structure, a few sessions at most per story. With Werewolf, I'm more leaning towards the method I used for the last big Forsaken chronicle I ran, that had four 'stories' across 2 years of play, each encapsulating the events that the pack experienced in sequential seasons. This, though, doesn't work so great with the greater focus on stories as mechanical units. I've also found that I sometimes prefer the leaner approach of shorter story arcs rather than the grand, sprawling, messy and organic approach under my last Forsaken campaign. I like downtime time-skips that can be slotted in between story arcs.<br /> <br /> I'm trying an experiment with the City of Light campaign that mixes and matches a bit between the two approaches. I currently have in mind two particular events that will see the end of the first story; if one of these happens, then the story is complete and there'll probably be a short gap before Story 2 continues. I haven't told the players these story-triggers. Currently, the triggers are either of:<br /> <br /> a) Defeating the Smoke Drinker<br /> b) Joining the Lamplighter or Zero Point protectorates.<br /> <br /> These are both significant milestones for the pack, so seem natural places to end the story. Of course, if events unfold such that both are likely to occur close to one another, I won't arbitrarily end the story after whichever occurs first.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in seeing how long the first story arc goes before one of these gets hit, or of course my mad players manage to instigate something else major enough to be an obvious end-point for the story arc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:33:08-07:00","id":511292,"title":"","content":"It says that the auspice abilities are once per chapter in the book which is usually a session no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2514-cathalramone","name":"cathalramone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2514_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:06:51-07:00","id":512235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cathalramone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=511292#post511292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says that the auspice abilities are once per chapter in the book which is usually a session no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just did a search and the only thing I could find that was limited per story is flashing your Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:07:05-07:00","id":512360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=512235#post512235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just did a search and the only thing I could find that was limited per story is flashing your Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean <b>flaring</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:10:16-07:00","id":512458,"title":"","content":"There's a setting book for Trail of Cthulhu (detective work in the Mythos set in the 1930s) called Dreamhounds of Paris. The idea is that a certain movement of artists begins to have a strange affect on the shape of the &quot;Dreamlands&quot; which I guess is the lovecraft version of the place of dreams. Seems to me the ideas expressed therein can just as easily apply to the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:23:58-07:00","id":512769,"title":"","content":"Oops. Funny thing is, I remember originally thinking they were once per session, then for some reason changing my belief to that they were once per story, and now I can't remember *why* I thought that.<br /> <br /> Checking this sort of stuff is going to be much easier once we have a print copy at the table and it isn't just me working off the pdf and my earlier-draft memories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=512458#post512458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a setting book for Trail of Cthulhu (detective work in the Mythos set in the 1930s) called Dreamhounds of Paris. The idea is that a certain movement of artists begins to have a strange affect on the shape of the &quot;Dreamlands&quot; which I guess is the lovecraft version of the place of dreams. Seems to me the ideas expressed therein can just as easily apply to the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I want to explore that kind of concept. For now, I'm holding off delving too deep into the artists/delirium/dreams concepts because the pack have a shitload of things on their plate to deal with already, but it'll likely be the focus of the second story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:20:21-07:00","id":514292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=512360#post512360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean <b>flaring</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the way I do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T02:15:20-07:00","id":519127,"title":"","content":"I've a quick question. I've noticed in the pod-casts that the guys are always really excited to get an exceptional success because it gives them a beat, is this a house rule? I can't find it in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5361-nicebrian","name":"NiceBrian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5361_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T04:20:22-07:00","id":519402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NiceBrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=519127#post519127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've a quick question. I've noticed in the pod-casts that the guys are always really excited to get an exceptional success because it gives them a beat, is this a house rule? I can't find it in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it works like this. Getting an Exceptional Success gets you a Condition. Resolving a Condition gets you a Beat. However, a) remembering to add the Beat at the time the Condition gets resolved is a pain, b) on-the-fly Conditions with short-term bonuses can sometimes then not actually be of any use because the scene just doesn't play out that way, missing out on the Beat unless the character does some really tortured logic to justify doing whatever will resolve the Condition, and c) it can get pretty tough to come up with decent Conditions for every Exceptional Success that's happening, especially when sometimes it's easier to give a non-Condition benefit instead.<br /> <br /> Thus, in order to keep the Beat generation from Exceptional-Success-created Conditions simple and straightforward, and not to punish the players if I give them a Condition for their Exceptional Success that turns out to not actually be useful, I just give the Beat when the Exceptional Success is rolled; but if they do get a Condition and resolve it, they don't then get a Beat from that, as they've already had it.<br /> <br /> I should probably write up a big list of quick-reference Conditions for common exceptional success types as well, would make it easier to handle Exceptional Sucesses in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T00:39:59-07:00","id":520691,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that makes perfect sense. I generally struggle with conditions, it's an aspect of the game that I'm still getting my head around, so that's probably where I failed to make the connection. Your method seems much simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5361-nicebrian","name":"NiceBrian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5361_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:37:22-07:00","id":525858,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the Nazi occupation of France and Paris, one can only imagine the kind of ugly they left behind especially their fascination with the occult.<br /> Also, those are Roman catacombs beneath the city if that inspires you. Perhaps your Idigam slumbers beneath a hidden temple of Hades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:23:57-07:00","id":535746,"title":"","content":"So in our last session the players encountered the other heretical sect (apart from the Apollonians) in Paris, the Drinkers from the Well.<br /> <br /> I'll get round to writing them up properly at some point, but suffice to say they are a previously Bone Shadow cult that worships and serves the Lou Carcohl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:42:33-07:00","id":535756,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I'm surprised to keep learning France has so much monster folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"